## 6. Test Design and Automation Framework

### 6.1 Playwright

Playwright is used for browser automation, UI interactions, assertions, and test execution. Its automatic waiting and locator-based assertions help reduce synchronization issues.

### 6.2 TypeScript

TypeScript provides static type checking and improves the maintainability of test scripts and reusable methods.

### 6.3 Page Object Model

The Page Object Model separates page-specific locators and actions from test scenarios.

The project contains page objects for:

- Login Page
- Inventory Page
- Cart Page
- Checkout Page
- Overview Page

This structure helps reduce code duplication and makes tests easier to update when page behavior or locators change.

### 6.4 Test Data Management

Reusable test data is maintained separately from test logic where appropriate.

The password is loaded from the `SAUCE_PASSWORD` environment variable rather than being embedded directly in test code.

### 6.5 Reporting

Playwright and Allure reporting are used to review test execution results and investigate failures.

