## 9. Exit Criteria

Testing for the planned scope can be considered complete when:

- All planned test cases have been executed or their execution status has been documented.
- Results have been reviewed and failures investigated.
- Critical workflow failures have been reported.
- Confirmed defects have sufficient reproduction details and supporting evidence where available.
- Known issues and expected failures have been clearly identified.
- The relevant execution reports have been generated and reviewed.
- Remaining coverage gaps and unresolved issues have been documented.

Passing all automated tests alone does not prove that every possible application scenario is defect-free.

